# Line endings.
#
# Git normally guesses, and the guess depends on each machine's core.autocrlf
# setting - so the same file can arrive differently on two Windows computers.
# For .bat that is not cosmetic: cmd.exe reads a batch file line by line as it
# runs it, and a file with Unix line endings can send `goto` to the wrong place
# or swallow the last line entirely. So the two launchers are pinned to CRLF
# and everything else to LF, whoever clones this and wherever from.

* text=auto

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.csv  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.ipynb text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
